        question: 'One mole of a real gas behaves according to the simplified Van der Waals equation of state: $P(V-b) = RT$. The gas undergoes a slow isothermal compression at temperature $T$ from an initial volume $V$ to a final volume of $V/2$. The work done on the gas by the external agent is:',
        options: ['$RT \\ln 2$', '$RT \\ln\\left(\\frac{V-b}{V/2-b}\\right)$', '$RT \\ln\\left(\\frac{2V-2b}{V-2b}\\right)$', '$RT \\ln\\left(\\frac{V}{V-2b}\\right)$'],
        correctAnswerIndex: 1,
        explanation: 'The work done by the gas during expansion is $W = \\int_{V_i}^{V_f} P dV = \\int_{V}^{V/2} \\frac{RT}{V-b} dV = RT \\ln\\left(\\frac{V/2-b}{V-b}\\right)$. Since it is compressed, the work done by the gas is negative. The work done ON the gas is the negative of work done by the gas: $W_{\\text{on}} = -W = RT \\ln\\left(\\frac{V-b}{V/2-b}\\right)$.'
